## 2. Typed Fetch Wrapper (`src/lib/api-client.ts`)

**File:** `D:\CLAUDE\Project\zakuppro\zakuppro\src\lib\api-client.ts`

The core function is `apiFetch<T>(endpoint, options)` which:
- Prefixes endpoints with `FASTAPI_URL` (env var or `http://localhost:8000`).
- Automatically attaches the JWT `Authorization: Bearer` header from `localStorage` (lines 157-162).
- Handles 401 by calling a pluggable `_onUnauthorized` callback (lines 199-201).
- Transforms FastAPI `{ "detail": ... }` error format into a standard `ApiError` (lines 95-117).
- Returns `ApiResult<T>` -- a discriminated union of `{ data: T | null, error: ApiError | null }` (lines 71-74).

Convenience helpers wrap `apiFetch` (lines 220-252):
```typescript
export async function get<T>(endpoint: string, params?): Promise<ApiResult<T>>
export async function post<T>(endpoint: string, body?: unknown): Promise<ApiResult<T>>
export async function put<T>(endpoint: string, body?: unknown): Promise<ApiResult<T>>
export async function patch<T>(endpoint: string, body?: unknown): Promise<ApiResult<T>>
export async function del<T>(endpoint: string): Promise<ApiResult<T>>
```

Additional utilities at lines 262-285:
```typescript
export function throwErrorOnError<T>(result: ApiResult<T>): T
export function isSuccess<T>(result: ApiResult<T>): result is ApiResult<T> & { data: T }
export function isFailure<T>(result: ApiResult<T>): result is ApiResult<T> & { error: ApiError }
```

