## 3. API Module Pattern (`src/lib/api/`)

**Directory listing of `D:\CLAUDE\Project\zakuppro\zakuppro\src\lib\api\`:**
```
analytics.ts
index.ts
invoices.ts
projects.ts
stock-items.ts
suppliers.ts
```

**Example -- `invoices.ts` (file: `D:\CLAUDE\Project\zakuppro\zakuppro\src\lib\api\invoices.ts`):**

Each API module follows this pattern:
```typescript
import { apiClient, type ApiResult } from '@/lib/api-client';
import type { /* relevant types */ } from '@/types/fastapi';

const BASE_PATH = '/api/invoices';       // (1) endpoint prefix

// (2) Named async functions, one per endpoint
export async function listInvoices(params?: ListQueryParams): Promise<ApiResult<InvoiceResponse[]>> {
  return apiClient.get<InvoiceResponse[]>(BASE_PATH, params);
}

export async function getInvoice(id: number): Promise<ApiResult<InvoiceResponse>> {
  return apiClient.get<InvoiceResponse>(`${BASE_PATH}/${id}`);
}

// ... create, update, delete ...

// (3) Grouped export object
export const invoicesApi = {
  list: listInvoices,
  get: getInvoice,
  create: createInvoice,
  update: updateInvoice,
  delete: deleteInvoice,
};

export default invoicesApi;
```

The `projects.ts` module follows the identical pattern, adding a `readiness` method.

