## 6. Sidebar Structure and Role Gating (`src/components/app/app-sidebar.tsx`)

**File:** `D:\CLAUDE\Project\zakuppro\zakuppro\src\components\app\app-sidebar.tsx`

**Nav items definition** (lines 38-53):
```typescript
const mainNavItems: { label: string; icon: React.ElementType; view: ViewType }[] = [
  { label: 'Дашборд', icon: LayoutDashboard, view: 'dashboard' },
  { label: 'Проекты', icon: FolderKanban, view: 'projects' },
  { label: 'Поставщики', icon: Building2, view: 'suppliers' },
  { label: 'Запросы', icon: Mail, view: 'requests' },
  { label: 'Счета', icon: FileText, view: 'invoices' },
  { label: 'Склад', icon: Warehouse, view: 'warehouse' },
  { label: 'Аналитика', icon: BarChart3, view: 'analytics' },
  { label: 'Автоматизация', icon: Zap, view: 'automation' },
]

const settingsNavItem = { label: 'Настройки', icon: Settings, view: 'settings' }
```

**Role-based gating** (lines 66-78):
```typescript
const { role } = useAuth()

const visibleMainNavItems = role
  ? mainNavItems.filter((item) => {
      if (role === 'owner') return true
      if (role === 'manager') return true
      if (role === 'warehouse') return item.view === 'dashboard' || item.view === 'warehouse'
      return true
    })
  : mainNavItems

const showSettings = role === 'owner'
```

The sidebar uses `'use client'`, imports `useAuth` from `@/components/providers/auth-provider`, and conditionally renders each item with active state, badges, and indicator dots. The `settings` view is only shown for `owner` role (line 192: `{showSettings && (...)}`).

